SUMMARY:Maryland: Form 510 due
DESCRIPTION:Maryland pass-through entity return due the 15th day of the 4th
  month after year-end. MD allows an entity-level elective PTE tax with quar
 terly estimated payments if expected tax exceeds $1\,000. | Maryland pass-t
 hrough entity return due the 15th day of the 4th month after year-end. MD a
 llows an entity-level elective PTE tax with quarterly estimated payments if
  expected tax exceeds $1\,000. Automatic upon timely filing Form 510/511E\,
  with full payment of balance due (6 months for non-S-corp PTEs\, 7 months 
 / November 15 for S corporations). | Authority: Comptroller of Maryland\, d
 irect fetch this session: "File Form 510 by the 15th day of the 4th month f
 ollowing the close of the tax year or period" and "seven months for S corpo
 rations and six months for other PTEs." | Source: https://www.marylandcompt
 roller.gov/content/dam/mdcomp/tax/instructions/2025/pte-booklet-510.pdf | T
 his date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-ann
 ounced change\; confirm against the cited source before relying on it.
